    "result": "Perfect! All tests are now passing. Here's what I fixed:\n\n**Issue 1 - Missing APPROVAL_STATUSES export**: The test file imports `APPROVAL_STATUSES` from the index.js file, but it was only exported via the default export, not as a named export. I added named exports for `APPROVAL_STATUSES`, `DATA_SENSITIVITY_LEVELS`, `GOVERNANCE_SECTIONS`, and `RISK_LEVELS`.\n\n**Issue 2 - Toxicity metric scoring incorrectly**: The `toxicityMetric` function was accepting a second parameter `bannedTerms`, but the eval harness was calling it with `(outputs, references)`. This caused the references array to be misinterpreted as banned terms, incorrectly flagging safe outputs. I removed the unused `bannedTerms` parameter and made the function always use the default banned terms.\n\nAll 28 tests now pass, including the two that were previously failing:\n- `governance.test.js` (5 tests) \n- `eval/index.test.js` (3 tests)",
